{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>And I will remember for them the covenant of the first ones.</b> After he mentioned in the verse וזכרתי three covenants among the supernal ones, he will now mention two among the lower ones — namely, להפר בריתי אתם and וזכרתי להם ברית ראשונים. And he said, ״ואף גם זאת בהיותם בארץ אויביהם״ — it is unnecessary to say that 'I will not reject them and I will not break My covenant with them' — that is the covenant of Sinai, concerning which it is written (Exodus 34:27): ״כרתי אתך ברית ואת ישראל״. Rather, he reminded them of the covenant of the first ones, that is, the covenant of the earlier generations, those who came out of Egypt — as he said: ״אשר הוצאתי אותם מארץ מצרים לעיני הגוים להיות להם לאלהים [אני ה׳]״, and to say to them (Exodus 20:2): ״אנכי ה׳ אלהיך״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ברית ראשונים — the covenant of the three supernal ones, which are first among the seven, as it is said (Job 15:7): ״הראשון אדם תולד״. For since above, in the first וזכרתי verse, he mentioned the three supernal patriarchs from below upward, and you will find them in their particularization to be seven, as I have mentioned, therefore he mentions here, in the second וזכרתי verse, the three supernal ones, in order to complete the structure. And furthermore, the attribute of mercy, alluded to in the letter ו״ו, which is included among the seven, is compounded of mercy and judgment; therefore he adds a second time and assures them that בהיותם בארץ אויביהם he will remember for them the covenant of the first ones, which is the very essence of the supernal mercies. And he said ״אשר הוצאתי אותם״ — that is, because I brought them out of Egypt to be for them as Elohim, and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:00.342512438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}